/*
 * assert-function-like.compact — assert is a function-like expression.
 *
 * Official release notes (do not invent APIs):
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/relnotes/compact/compact-0-16-24-0
 * In Compact 0.14 and before, assert was a statement:
 *   assert age() >= 18 "failed age check";
 * From Compact 0.16.0 it is a function-like expression operator:
 *   assert(age() >= 18, "failed age check");
 *
 * Official writing guide still shows the new form:
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/compact/reference/writing
 *
 * Upstream: https://github.com/midnightntwrk/midnight-docs/issues/1487
 * Test-and-debug samples use older shapes that do not compile under the pin.
 * This lab pin is Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
 * Source only. Not compiled. No on-chain deploy is claimed.
 *
 * Built by @kshot9000 https://x.com/kshot9000
 * Email: kshot9000@gmail.com
